title: 'statement-store: split the v2 inbound statement slots by peer role'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    With the v2 DHT path on, the statement set gets the node's light allowance on top of its
    inbound slots and the handler splits them by role, so a light peer is admitted while the full
    slots are taken. A reserved peer holds no slot. The full slots come from the new
    `--statement-in-peers` flag, 50 by default. `StatementHandlerPrototype::new` takes the network
    configuration and the v2 DHT configuration as new arguments.
crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: major
- name: sc-statement-store
  bump: minor
- name: staging-node-cli
  bump: minor
- name: polkadot-omni-node-lib
  bump: major
